CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*jlm2)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct static_key_mod)...)
#275: FILE: kernel/jump_label.c:481:
+			jlm2 = kzalloc(sizeof(struct static_key_mod),

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

CHECK:COMPARISON_TO_NULL: Comparison to NULL could be written "!jlm->next"
#324: FILE: kernel/jump_label.c:546:
+		if (jlm->next == NULL) {

Comparisons to NULL in the form (foo == NULL) or (foo != NULL)
are better written as (!foo) and (foo).

